Chapter: BvtPowderCities
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter CityWorkers
  cites Uoaix chapter Cities
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 UOAIX-242 D6, root's reading of "powders need demand" (2026-10-14): each town's smith serves its own guards from its own
 stock, so Nujel'm's powders (dug there, sold to Nujel'm's smith) meet Nujel'm's guards.
  bpc-smiths : Integer -> Boolean
  bpc-smiths (unused) = let nujelm = cw-nujelm (ct-table 0) (ct-city-shops 0) ct-shop-roles
    in let skara = cw-skara (ct-table 0) (ct-city-shops 0) ct-shop-roles
    in let n = cw-vendor nujelm cg-armory
    in let s = cw-vendor skara cg-armory
    in let listed = cg-smiths-from [cw-britain, nujelm, skara] 0 [cg-armory]
    in n >= bb-shop-count & s >= bb-shop-count & n /= s & list-length listed == 3 & list-at listed 0 == cg-armory
      & cg-int-in listed n 0 & cg-int-in listed s 0
  bpc-patrol-city : List CtPatrol, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  bpc-patrol-city (ps) (city) (i) = if i >= list-length ps then False else if (list-at ps i).city == city then True else bpc-patrol-city ps city (i + 1)
  bvt-powder-cities : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-powder-cities (unused) = act
    a <- bvt-check "every town's smith is counted once, Britain's armory first: Britain, Nujel'm and Skara Brae give 3 smiths, Nujel'm's and Skara Brae's city shops (cg-smiths-from)" (bpc-smiths 0)
    b <- bvt-check "Nujel'm, the one town that digs powder, has guards for its smith to serve (ct-city-patrols city 8)" (bpc-patrol-city (ct-city-patrols 0) 8 0)
    c <- bvt-check "Britain listed twice is one smith, and an empty city list leaves Britain's alone (cg-smiths-from, cg-int-in)" (list-length (cg-smiths-from [cw-britain, cw-britain] 0 [cg-armory]) == 1 & list-length (cg-smiths-from [] 0 [cg-armory]) == 1 & not (cg-int-in [1, 2] 3 0))
    a + b + c
  end
